// diag_pos_stmt_reject: a statement-level diagnostic must land on the line
// of the OFFENDING statement, not the line of the next token.
//
// The parser had no location tracking: get_current_position()
// (parser_actions.c) returned current_lexer->pos, the LIVE lexer cursor,
// which by the time a bison reduction action runs holds the position of the
// LOOKAHEAD token bison has already read. So this fixture's error was
// reported at line 19 (`_ = s`) instead of line 18 (`var s string = 5`).
//
// The sidecar pins the LINE only. Column precision for the offending
// sub-expression (Go points at the `5`, column 17) depends on migrating the
// literal/expression constructors, a later batch — this batch moves
// statement and declaration nodes onto bison's @$ locations, whose column is
// the construct's own start (`var`).
package main

func main() {
	var s string = 5
	_ = s
}
